{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794808024206,"sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2e4ec26002tIp9jMG26T4LtR","sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","messageID":"msg_1e2e4db68001Nq1gXjUsCpdHxA","type":"tool","id":"call_00_vp70vys8k12vh2n6pn6vp420","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - OpenCode/Pi Session Hand-Over Parity\ndescription: Runtime strategy for the opencode-go-deepseek detached fan-out lineage of the 011 OpenCode/Pi hand-over parity packet.\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for this lineage's research run. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read at every iteration; machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer.\n\n### Mutability\n\nAnalyst-owned sections stay stable. Sections 3, 6, 7-11A are rewritten by `reduce-state.cjs` from the registry after each iteration.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nFind every reason a session hand-over hop on OpenCode or Pi can fail to finish the sender's task, or fail to recover a detail the note left out through the History Lookup, and name a concrete fix for each. Known case: a live Pi hop on DeepSeek V4.1 Flash at max scored 4/5. The sender kept a side word out of its note as told, then wrote that a fresh session could not recover it. The receiver was offered a working History Lookup, did not run it, asked the operator and left the note claimed. The same task on OpenCode scored 5/5.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] What does each runtime's prepare text tell the sender about keeping details out of the note, and does it over-promise what a fresh session can recover through the History Lookup?\n- [ ] What claim text and History Lookup offer does the receiver read on OpenCode versus Pi, and what makes a receiver leave a claim unverified instead of running the lookup?\n- [ ] How do the OpenCode and Pi session readers feed the History Lookup, including their tool-call argument shapes and secret redaction, and what does each fail to recover?\n- [ ] Does model and effort carry on relaunch for each runtime, and where can it silently degrade or be dropped?\n- [ ] Which known limits (OpenCode store without a directory column, AI_SESSION_CHILD leaking into test sandboxes, the 160-character preview cut, a double nudge from two hooks) cause a hop to fail, and what concrete fix addresses each?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Implementing the fixes. This run reports findings and concrete fix proposals only.\n- Re-scoring the live Pi/OpenCode runs in `scratch/runs/`; their scorecards are evidence, not targets.\n- Auditing unrelated hook subsystems (git, spec-gate, skill-advisor) except where they change hand-over behaviour.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- All five key questions answered with cited evidence and a named fix per failure mode.\n- Two consecutive iterations with `newInfoRatio` at or below 0.05 after the minimum-iteration floor clears.\n- `maxIterations` (10) reached.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[Populated as directions are eliminated]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n\nIteration 1: read the prepare text each runtime gives the sender (`.skilled/hooks/session-handover/` per-runtime prepare assets and `.pi/extensions/session-handover.ts`) and compare it to what the receiver is told it can recover, so the over-promise that produced the Pi 4/5 case is pinned to a line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n- Hand-over hook family: `.skilled/hooks/session-handover/` with per-runtime subdirectories (`claude/`, `codex/`, `opencode/`, `pi/`, `vibe/`), shared `lib/`, `history/` (the History Lookup), and `bin/`.\n- Shared session readers: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/` (claude, codex, cursor, devin, dsh, identity, index).\n- Pi extension surface: `.pi/extensions/session-handover.ts`.\n- OpenCode plugin surface: `.opencode/plugins/` (notably `session-handover.js`, plus adjacent plugins that can double-fire a nudge).\n- Live run evidence: `specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/` containing `base1-pi` and `base1-opencode` notes, panes, meta and scorecards.\n- Known limits named in the charter: OpenCode store without a directory column; `AI_SESSION_CHILD` leaking into test sandboxes; 160-character preview cut; double nudge from two hooks.\n- `resource-map.md` not present; skipping coverage gate.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n\n- Max iterations: 10\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research/research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-16T05:46:33Z\n","path":"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - OpenCode/Pi Session Hand-Over Parity\\ndescription: Runtime strategy for the opencode-go-deepseek detached fan-out lineage of the 011 OpenCode/Pi hand-over parity packet.\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - Session Tracking\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for this lineage's research run. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next. Read at every iteration; machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer.\\n\\n### Mutability\\n\\nAnalyst-owned sections stay stable. Sections 3, 6, 7-11A are rewritten by `reduce-state.cjs` from the registry after each iteration.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nFind every reason a session hand-over hop on OpenCode or Pi can fail to finish the sender's task, or fail to recover a detail the note left out through the History Lookup, and name a concrete fix for each. Known case: a live Pi hop on DeepSeek V4.1 Flash at max scored 4/5. The sender kept a side word out of its note as told, then wrote that a fresh session could not recover it. The receiver was offered a working History Lookup, did not run it, asked the operator and left the note claimed. The same task on OpenCode scored 5/5.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n\\n- [ ] What does each runtime's prepare text tell the sender about keeping details out of the note, and does it over-promise what a fresh session can recover through the History Lookup?\\n- [ ] What claim text and History Lookup offer does the receiver read on OpenCode versus Pi, and what makes a receiver leave a claim unverified instead of running the lookup?\\n- [ ] How do the OpenCode and Pi session readers feed the History Lookup, including their tool-call argument shapes and secret redaction, and what does each fail to recover?\\n- [ ] Does model and effort carry on relaunch for each runtime, and where can it silently degrade or be dropped?\\n- [ ] Which known limits (OpenCode store without a directory column, AI_SESSION_CHILD leaking into test sandboxes, the 160-character preview cut, a double nudge from two hooks) cause a hop to fail, and what concrete fix addresses each?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Implementing the fixes. This run reports findings and concrete fix proposals only.\\n- Re-scoring the live Pi/OpenCode runs in `scratch/runs/`; their scorecards are evidence, not targets.\\n- Auditing unrelated hook subsystems (git, spec-gate, skill-advisor) except where they change hand-over behaviour.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- All five key questions answered with cited evidence and a named fix per failure mode.\\n- Two consecutive iterations with `newInfoRatio` at or below 0.05 after the minimum-iteration floor clears.\\n- `maxIterations` (10) reached.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n[Populated as directions are eliminated]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n\\n[Populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\n\\nIteration 1: read the prepare text each runtime gives the sender (`.skilled/hooks/session-handover/` per-runtime prepare assets and `.pi/extensions/session-handover.ts`) and compare it to what the receiver is told it can recover, so the over-promise that produced the Pi 4/5 case is pinned to a line.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CO