udge will come once the context'\n49:   + ' fills further. That nudge is when to update the note and hand over again. Do not run'\n50:   + ' consume or claim by hand.';\n51: const DEFAULT_THRESHOLD = 0.8;\n52: // The wrapper's own ceiling on completed hops, used when no cap is configured.\n53: const DEFAULT_MAX_HOPS = core.DEFAULT_MAX_HOPS;\n54: const SESSION_ID_PATTERN = /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$/;\n55: // Notes named before the full id went into the filename carry this many leading id\n56: // characters; the reader still accepts them so a note written then keeps its work.\n57: const LEGACY_SESSION_ID_PREFIX_LENGTH = 8;\n58: const FINISH_INSTEAD_INSTRUCTION = ' If the remaining work fits in a few more steps, finish it instead'\n59:   + ' and skip these steps.'\n60:   + ' Otherwise do these steps now, before any other work,'\n61:   + ' so a fresh session continues before auto-compaction has to:';\n62: // Outside the wrapper nothing can relaunch the session, but a note still keeps what the\n63: // compaction summary loses, so the session writes one, keeps it, and carries on.\n64: const OUTSIDE_LOOP_INSTRUCTION = ' This session runs outside the skilled-loop wrapper, so it'\n65:   + ' cannot relaunch; a handoff note keeps the exact decisions auto-compaction would summarize.'\n66:   + ' If the remaining work fits in a few more steps, finish it instead and skip these steps.'\n67:   + ' Otherwise do these steps now, before any other work:';\n68: // A receiver re-runs the note's active command, so it checks every worker the note names\n69: // first: a live worker already owns that work.\n70: const WORKER_CHECK_INSTRUCTION = ' Before you run the active command again, run `kill -0 <pid>`'\n71:   + ' for each worker the note\\'s `Running workers:` line names; when a pid is alive, collect'\n72:   + ' its worker with the collect step from that line instead of starting the same work again,'\n73:   + ' and do not re-run the active command while a listed worker runs.';\n74: // A hop ends the runtime that held the schedules and the added directories; a compaction kept\n75: // both, so only a hop seed rebuilds them.\n76: const HOP_RESTORE_INSTRUCTION = ' After a hop, recreate each `Scheduled:` entry the note lists,'\n77:   + ' or tell the operator which to recreate when this runtime has no scheduler, and re-add'\n78:   + ' each `Added directories:` entry, or ask the operator to (on Claude Code,'\n79:   + ' `/add-dir <path>`).';\n80: \n81: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n82: // 3. HELPERS\n83: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n84: \n85: function shellQuote(value) {\n86:   const quote = String.fromCharCode(39);\n87:   const escapedQuote = quote + '\"' + quote + '\"' + quote;\n88:   return quote + String(value).replace(/'/g, escapedQuote) + quote;\n89: }\n90: \n91: // A session id or a cwd is copied into the note frontmatter, so every C0 control character\n92: // and DEL comes out before it is printed: a line break there would add a field the operator\n93: // never wrote. The stripped value no longer matches the real session or folder, which is\n94: // why prepare refuses a note built from it.\n95: function stripControlCharacters(value) {\n96:   return String(value).replace(/[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f]/g, '');\n97: }\n98: \n99: // The printed command is text the model runs, so a value that starts with node passes\n100: // through only as one invocation of one argument with no shell syntax in it: a\n101: // single-quoted string without a quote inside, or a run of characters the shell reads as\n102: // data. Anything else is quoted whole, so it can only ever be the path of the command.\n103: function commandPrefix(cliPath) {\n104:   if (typeof cliPath !== 'string' || !cliPath.trim()) return CLI_COMMAND;\n105:   const nodeInvocation = /^node +(.*)$/s.exec(cliPath);\n106:   if (nodeInvocation !== null) {\n107:     const argument = nodeInvocation[1];\n108:     if (/^'[^']*'$/.test(argument) || /^[A-Za-z0-9_/.@:+-]+$/.test(argument)) return cliPath;\n109:   }\n110:   return `node ${shellQuote(cliPath)}`;\n111: }\n112: \n113: /** Build the command that closes a handoff note, shared by seed text and every reminder. */\n114: function completeCommandFor(notePath, cliPath) {\n115:   const pathValue = String(notePath ?? '<handoff-path>');\n116:   return `${commandPrefix(cliPath)} complete ${shellQuote(pathValue)}`;\n117: }\n118: \n119: /** Build the command that claims a handoff note for a session. */\n120: function claimCommandFor(notePath, sessionId, cliPath) {\n121:   const pathValue = String(notePath ?? '<handoff-path>');\n122:   return `${commandPrefix(cliPath)} claim ${shellQuote(pathValue)}`\n123:     + ` --session ${shellQuote(String(sessionId ?? ''))}`;\n124: }\n125: \n126: // A window override can push the measured ratio far past 1, so the literal percentage\n127: // reads as a broken hook to the model receiving it; name the overflow instead.\n128: function contextSentence(ratio) {\n129:   if (typeof ratio !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(ratio)) return null;\n130:   return ratio > 1\n131:     ? `${SEED_PREFIX} Context is past the configured window (over 100% full).`\n132:     : `${SEED_PREFIX} Context is about ${Math.round(ratio * 100)}% full.`;\n133: }\n134: \n135: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n136: // 4. CORE LOGIC\n137: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n138: \n139: /**\n140:  * Reduce a spec-folder answer to one prepare accepts: empty when unanswered, `none` for a\n141:  * Gate 3 skip, or a valid packet path. Anything else, including a value that would add\n142:  * frontmatter lines, is unknown and returns undefined.\n143:  */\n144: function normalizeSpecFolder(value) {\n145:   if (value === '' || value === 'none') return value;\n146:   return core.validSpecFolder(value) ? value : undefined;\n147: }\n148: \n149: // No host puts a spec folder in its hook payload today, so the payload field stays a\n150: // seam for one that does, and the session's bound packet comes from SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER.\n151: // An empty variable says nothing about the answer, so it reads as unknown.\n152: /** Resolve the spec folder a nudge writes into the note, payload first. */\n153: function specFolderInput({ payload, env = process.env } = {}) {\n154:   const fromPayload = normalizeSpecFolder(payload?.spec_folder);\n155:   if (fromPayload !== undefined) return fromPayload;\n156:   const fromEnvironment = env?.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n157:   return fromEnvironment ? normalizeSpecFolder(fromEnvironment) : undefined;\n158: }\n159: \n160: /** Build the context handoff instructions for a runtime nudge. */\n161: function handoffText({\n162:   notePath,\n163:   sessionId,\n164:   specFolder,\n165:   runtime = 'claude',\n166:   cliPath,\n167:   cwd = process.cwd(),\n168:   loopId = process.env.SKILLED_LOOP_ID || '',\n169:   createdAt = new Date().toISOString(),\n170:   ratio,\n171: } = {}) {\n172:   const pathValue = String(notePath ?? '<handoff-path>');\n173:   const sessionValue = stripControlCharacters(sessionId ?? '');\n174:   const cwdValue = stripControlCharacters(cwd);\n175:   // An unknown folder prints empty: the guidance line tells the model what may go there,\n176:   // and a placeholder copied verbatim is a value prepare rejects.\n177:   const folder = normalizeSpecFolder(specFolder);\n178:   const specValue = folder ?? '';\n179:   const command = commandPrefix(cliPath);\n180:   const context = contextSentence(ratio);\n181:   const inLoop = Boolean(loopId);\n182:   let opening = `${SEED_PREFIX} Write a handoff note before auto-compaction.`;\n183:   if (context !== null) {\n184:     opening = context + (inLoop ? FINISH_INSTEAD_INSTRUCTION : OUTSIDE_LOOP_INSTRUCTION);\n185:   }\n186:   // The sections asked for are the ones validateHandoff enforces, so prepare accepts the note.\n187:   const sectionList = core.HANDOFF_SECTIONS.map((name) => `## ${name}`).join(', ');\n188:   const activeGoalInstruction = runtime === 'codex'\n189:     ? ' For Codex, also include an `Active goal:` line with the goal or packet path; use '\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 190]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs, lines 30-189\n30:   + 'section states the problem, so it is never the purpose. When the text is empty, UNKNOWN, a '\n31:   + 'template placeholder or a scaffold sentence that begins Keep parent documentation lean or '\n32:   + 'This phase groups the related child phases below, use the nearest phase parent that has one '\n33:   + 'and write `Parent purpose (<repo-relative parent folder>): <sentence>`. '\n34:   + 'When neither exists and the packet holds a goal.md, write `Goal objective: <sentence>` from '\n35:   + 'its Objective. Leave the line out when there is no such text. Then say what this session '\n36:   + 'works toward.';\n37: // Every adapter prints this command, so the model always runs the CLI from the repo root.\n38: const CLI_COMMAND = 'node .skilled/hooks/session-handover/bin/session-handover.cjs';\n39: const CONTINUITY_WRITER_COMMAND = 'node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/'\n40:   + 'dist/continuity/generate-context.js';\n41: const NUDGE_STEP = 0.05;\n42: const LAST_NUDGE_LEVEL = 1;\n43: // What a session is told when its prepared hand-over was withdrawn by a prompt: the prompt\n44: // itself carries this and nothing else, because a nudge on the same turn would ask for the\n45: // hand-over the session was just freed from.\n46: const WITHDRAWN_NOTICE = '[session-handover] The prepared hand-over was withdrawn because'\n47:   + ' a new prompt arrived before it took effect. Keep working here. The open'\n48:   + ' note no longer matches the work, and one more context nudge will come once the context'\n49:   + ' fills further. That nudge is when to update the note and hand over again. Do not run'\n50:   + ' consume or claim by hand.';\n51: const DEFAULT_THRESHOLD = 0.8;\n52: // The wrapper's own ceiling on completed hops, used when no cap is configured.\n53: const DEFAULT_MAX_HOPS = core.DEFAULT_MAX_HOPS;\n54: const SESSION_ID_PATTERN = /^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}$/;\n55: // Notes named before the full id went into the filename carry this many leading id\n56: // characters; the reader still accepts them so a note written then keeps its work.\n57: const LEGACY_SESSION_ID_PREFIX_LENGTH = 8;\n58: const FINISH_INSTEAD_INSTRUCTION = ' If the remaining work fits in a few more steps, finish it instead'\n59:   + ' and skip these steps.'\n60:   + ' Otherwise do these steps now, before any other work,'\n61:   + ' so a fresh session continues before auto-compaction has to:';\n62: // Outside the wrapper nothing can relaunch the session, but a note still keeps what the\n63: // compaction summary loses, so the session writes one, keeps it, and carries on.\n64: const OUTSIDE_LOOP_INSTRUCTION = ' This session runs outside the skilled-loop wrapper, so it'\n65:   + ' cannot relaunch; a handoff note keeps the exact decisions auto-compaction would summarize.'\n66:   + ' If the remaining work fits in a few more steps, finish it instead and skip these steps.'\n67:   + ' Otherwise do these steps now, before any other work:';\n68: // A receiver re-runs the note's active command, so it checks every worker the note names\n69: // first: a live worker already owns that work.\n70: const WORKER_CHECK_INSTRUCTION = ' Before you run the active command again, run `kill -0 <pid>`'\n71:   + ' for each worker the note\\'s `Running workers:` line names; when a pid is alive, collect'\n72:   + ' its worker with the collect step from that line instead of starting the same work again,'\n73:   + ' and do not re-run the active command while a listed worker runs.';\n74: // A hop ends the runtime that held the schedules and the added directories; a compaction kept\n75: // both, so only a hop seed rebuilds them.\n76: const HOP_RESTORE_INSTRUCTION = ' After a hop, recreate each `Scheduled:` entry the note lists,'\n77:   + ' or tell the operator which to recreate when this runtime has no scheduler, and re-add'\n78:   + ' each `Added directories:` entry, or ask the operator to (on Claude Code,'\n79:   + ' `/add-dir <path>`).';\n80: \n81: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n82: // 3. HELPERS\n83: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n84: \n85: function shellQuote(value) {\n86:   const quote = String.fromCharCode(39);\n87:   const escapedQuote = quote + '\"' + quote + '\"' + quote;\n88:   return quote + String(value).replace(/'/g, escapedQuote) + quote;\n89: }\n90: \n91: // A session id or a cwd is copied into the note frontmatter, so every C0 control character\n92: // and DEL comes out before it is printed: a line break there would add a field the operator\n93: // never wrote. The stripped value no longer matches the real session or folder, which is\n94: // why prepare refuses a note built from it.\n95: function stripControlCharacters(value) {\n96:   return String(value).replace(/[\\u0000-\\u001f\\u007f]/g, '');\n97: }\n98: \n99: // The printed command is text the model runs, so a value that starts with node passes\n100: // through only as one invocation of one argument with no shell syntax in it: a\n101: // single-quoted string without a quote inside, or a run of characters the shell reads as\n102: // data. Anything else is quoted whole, so it can only ever be the path of the command.\n103: function commandPrefix(cliPath) {\n104:   if (typeof cliPath !== 'string' || !cliPath.trim()) return CLI_COMMAND;\n105:   const nodeInvocation = /^node +(.*)$/s.exec(cliPath);\n106:   if (nodeInvocation !== null) {\n107:     const argument = nodeInvocation[1];\n108:     if (/^'[^']*'$/.test(argument) || /^[A-Za-z0-9_/.@:+-]+$/.test(argument)) return cliPath;\n109:   }\n110:   return `node ${shellQuote(cliPath)}`;\n111: }\n112: \n113: /** Build the command that closes a handoff note, shared by seed text and every reminder. */\n114: function completeCommandFor(notePath, cliPath) {\n115:   const pathValue = String(notePath ?? '<handoff-path>');\n116:   return `${commandPrefix(cliPath)} complete ${shellQuote(pathValue)}`;\n117: }\n118: \n119: /** Build the command that claims a handoff note for a session. */\n120: function claimCommandFor(notePath, sessionId, cliPath) {\n121:   const pathValue = String(notePath ?? '<handoff-path>');\n122:   return `${commandPrefix(cliPath)} claim ${shellQuote(pathValue)}`\n123:     + ` --session ${shellQuote(String(sessionId ?? ''))}`;\n124: }\n125: \n126: // A window override can push the measured ratio far past 1, so the literal percentage\n127: // reads as a broken hook to the model receiving it; name the overflow instead.\n128: function contextSentence(ratio) {\n129:   if (typeof ratio !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(ratio)) return null;\n130:   return ratio > 1\n131:     ? `${SEED_PREFIX} Context is past the configured window (over 100% full).`\n132:     : `${SEED_PREFIX} Context is about ${Math.round(ratio * 100)}% full.`;\n133: }\n134: \n135: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n136: // 4. CORE LOGIC\n137: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n138: \n139: /**\n140:  * Reduce a spec-folder answer to one prepare accepts: empty when unanswered, `none` for a\n141:  * Gate 3 skip, or a valid packet path. Anything else, including a value that would add\n142:  * frontmatter lines, is unknown and returns undefined.\n143:  */\n144: function normalizeSpecFolder(value) {\n145:   if (value === '' || value === 'none') return value;\n146:   return core.validSpecFolder(value) ? value : undefined;\n147: }\n148: \n149: // No host puts a spec folder in its hook payload today, so the payload field stays a\n150: // seam for one that does, and the session's bound packet comes from SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER.\n151: // An empty variable says nothing about the answer, so it reads as unknown.\n152: /** Resolve the spec folder a nudge writes into the note, payload first. */\n153: function specFolderInput({ payload, env = process.env } = {}) {\n154:   const fromPayload = normalizeSpecFolder(payload?.spec_folder);\n155:   if (fromPayload !== undefined) return fromPayload;\n156:   const fromEnvironment = env?.SYSTEM_SPEC_FOLDER;\n157:   return fromEnvironment ? normalizeSpecFolder(fromEnvironment) : undefined;\n158: }\n159: \n160: /** Build the context handoff instructions for a runtime nudge. */\n161: function handoffText({\n162:   notePath,\n163:   sessionId,\n164:   specFolder,\n165:   runtime = 'claude',\n166:   cliPath,\n167:   cwd = process.cwd(),\n168:   loopId = process.env.SKILLED_LOOP_ID || '',\n169:   createdAt = new Date().toISOString(),\n170:   ratio,\n171: } = {}) {\n172:   const pathValue = String(notePath ?? '<handoff-path>');\n173:   const sessionValue = stripControlCharacters(sessionId ?? '');\n174:   const cwdValue = stripControlCharacters(cwd);\n175:   // An unknown folder prints empty: the guidance line tells the model what may go there,\n176:   // and a placeholder copied verbatim is a value prepare rejects.\n177:   const folder = normalizeSpecFolder(specFolder);\n178:   const specValue = folder ?? '';\n179:   const command = commandPrefix(cliPath);\n180:   const context = contextSentence(ratio);\n181:   const inLoop = Boolean(loopId);\n182:   let opening = `${SEED_PREFIX} Write a handoff note before auto-compaction.`;\n183:   if (context !== null) {\n184:     opening = context + (inLoop ? FINISH_INSTEAD_INSTRUCTION : OUTSIDE_LOOP_INSTRUCTION);\n185:   }\n186:   // The sections asked for are the ones validateHandoff enforces, so prepare accepts the note.\n187:   const sectionList = core.HANDOFF_SECTIONS.map((name) => `## ${name}`).join(', ');\n188:   const activeGoalInstruction = runtime === 'codex'\n189:     ? ' For Codex, also include an `Active goal:` line with the goal or packet path; use '\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 190]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 160, \"offset\": 30, \"path\": \".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794808052178,"end":1794808052871}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794808052877,"sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2e57ac2001MM6eLbafDfD1jo","sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","messageID":"msg_1e2e57017001rQ6FClou1OiwS7","type":"tool","id":"call_01_1dfmt37r2y3ok7lpv3cci221","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"History Lookup|history lookup|history-lookup|lookup offer|LOOKUP","path":".skilled/hooks/session-handover","include":"*.{cjs,mjs,ts,md}","limit":60},"output":"Found 60 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity/.skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/relaunch-core.cjs:\n  Line 1058:  * Build the history lookup section a claim prints for the session that wrote the note.\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity/.skilled/hooks/session-handover/bin/history-lookup.mjs:\n  Line 2: // MODULE: History Lookup Entry\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity/.skilled/hooks/session-handover/README.md:\n  Line 17: The `session-handover/` folder holds the shared handoff logic, one adapter per automatic runtime, the CLI and the tests for the session handover loop. It also holds the history lookup: `bin/history-lookup.mjs`, the runnable entry for the printed lookup command, and `history/`, the engine that reads the sender's earlier turns back. Section 3 explains how the lookup works end to end. Each adapter asks for a handoff near its context threshold. The sender prepares a note and the adapter arms a matching record. After the runtime exits, `skilled-loop` relaunches it with a claim seed when the record is armed, fresh and below the hop cap. If a record is still pending at exit, the wrapper prints a manual claim command for the selected runtime and consumes the record. `SKILLED_LOOP_MANUAL_TEMPLATE` builds that command from the first launch's name and Pi extension flags, and from the model, provider and effort the record carries when it has them, so after a hop that switched model the printed command names the model the session was last using. The killer uses the same template in its timeout notification.\n\n  Line 198: ### History Lookup After A Claim\n\n  Line 200: A handoff note holds what the sender chose to write down. The history lookup gives the receiver a way to read the sender's own earlier turns for a detail the note left out, such as an exact code, a path or a figure, instead of guessing it.\n\n  Line 202: **What the claim prints.** `claim` mints a history locator for the sending session with provenance source `handover` and prints a `## History Lookup` section after the note body, then the sentence `Use it for a detail this note does not spell out, before you guess.` The section names one read-only command, `node .skilled/hooks/session-handover/bin/history-lookup.mjs --session <id> --handle <hl1_...> <operation> <json>`, which searches, browses, loads and pages the sender's earlier turns. The command runs in a subshell that first moves to the checkout root, so it works from any subfolder. A locator from any sender other than Claude Code adds its runtime in front of it, such as `SPECKIT_RUNTIME=codex` or `SPECKIT_RUNTIME=pi`.\n\n  Line 398: |   `-- history-lookup.mjs   (the entry the printed lookup command runs)\n\n  Line 399: +-- history/                 (the history lookup engine, see history/README.md)\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity/.skilled/hooks/session-handover/tests/history-lookup-entry.test.cjs:\n  Line 2: // MODULE: Session Handover History Lookup Entry Tests\n\n  Line 14: const ENTRY_PATH = path.join(__dirname, '..', 'bin', 'history-lookup.mjs');\n\n  Line 16: const ENTRY_RELATIVE_PATH = '.skilled/hooks/session-handover/bin/history-lookup.mjs';\n\n  Line 26:   const root = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'history-lookup-entry-'));\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity/.skilled