ing.',\n266:     );\n267:   }\n268:   lines.push(\n269:     'Exception: skip these steps only when the operator has told this session not to hand off;'\n270:       + ' then keep working, and auto-compaction stays the fallback.',\n271:   );\n272:   return lines.join('\\n');\n273: }\n274: \n275: /** Build the claim, resume, and completion instructions for a seed prompt. */\n276: function seedText({\n277:   notePath,\n278:   specFolder,\n279:   sessionId,\n280:   cliPath,\n281:   afterCompaction = false,\n282:   createdAt,\n283: } = {}) {\n284:   const pathValue = String(notePath ?? '<handoff-path>');\n285:   const claimCommand = claimCommandFor(pathValue, sessionId, cliPath);\n286:   const completeCommand = completeCommandFor(pathValue, cliPath);\n287:   const gateWasSkipped = specFolder === 'none';\n288:   let continueStep = gateWasSkipped ? 4 : 3;\n289:   let readInstruction = '2. Read the note.' + WORKER_CHECK_INSTRUCTION;\n290:   if (typeof specFolder === 'string' && specFolder && !gateWasSkipped) {\n291:     readInstruction = '2. Read the note. When its frontmatter spec_folder is set, run '\n292:       + `\\`/speckit:resume ${specFolder}\\`; skip that step when spec_folder is empty.`\n293:       + WORKER_CHECK_INSTRUCTION;\n294:   }\n295: \n296:   const lines = [\n297:     afterCompaction\n298:       ? '[session-handover] This session was compacted after it wrote a handoff note, which'\n299:         + ' keeps the detail the summary dropped. Work it in order:'\n300:       : '[session-handover] This session was opened to continue a handoff note. Work it in order:',\n301:     `1. Run \\`${claimCommand}\\`; it prints the note body.`,\n302:     readInstruction,\n303:   ];\n304:   if (gateWasSkipped) {\n305:     lines.push('3. Gate 3 is already answered Skip for this session, carried from the handoff.');\n306:   }\n307:   lines.push(\n308:     `${continueStep}. If the note has an \\`Active goal:\\` line other than \\`none\\`, use `\n309:       + '`create_goal` to bring that goal back into this session. On a runtime without '\n310:       + '`create_goal`, tell the operator which goal to set.',\n311:   );\n312:   continueStep += 1;\n313:   if (typeof specFolder === 'string' && specFolder && !gateWasSkipped) {\n314:     lines.push(\n315:       `${continueStep}. When ${specFolder}/goal.md exists, read it before Remaining work; `\n316:         + 'its durable directive binds the session goal.',\n317:     );\n318:     continueStep += 1;\n319:   }\n320:   lines.push(\n321:     `${continueStep}. When the note's \\`Active command:\\` line names a command, run it again `\n322:       + 'with the same mode and arguments; the command\\'s own state detection picks the step. '\n323:       + 'Skip this when the line says `none`.',\n324:   );\n325:   continueStep += 1;\n326:   // A session that kept working after it wrote the note may have committed some of its\n327:   // Remaining work since, so it checks git before trusting the list. The note date is the\n328:   // boundary for that check; without one the step still asks for the history.\n329:   if (afterCompaction) {\n330:     const dated = typeof createdAt === 'string' && createdAt.trim() !== '';\n331:     lines.push(dated\n332:       ? `${continueStep}. The note was written at ${createdAt}. Run `\n333:         + `\\`git log --since=${shellQuote(createdAt)}\\` and \\`git status\\`, and compare them `\n334:         + 'with Remaining work before you trust it.'\n335:       : `${continueStep}. Run \\`git log\\` and \\`git status\\`, and compare them with Remaining `\n336:         + 'work before you trust it; work committed after the note was written is already done.');\n337:     continueStep += 1;\n338:   }\n339:   lines.push(\n340:     `${continueStep}. Continue the work under \"Remaining work\". Do not run prepare for this note; `\n341:       + 'its handoff is already done. If Remaining work names only handoff steps, '\n342:       + 'treat it as empty.',\n343:     `${continueStep + 1}. When the remaining work is done, run `\n344:       + `\\`${completeCommand}\\` to close the note.`\n345:       + (afterCompaction ? '' : HOP_RESTORE_INSTRUCTION),\n346:   );\n347:   return lines.join('\\n');\n348: }\n349: \n350: /**\n351:  * Build the compaction text for a session whose hand-over was withdrawn. Its open note was\n352:  * written before the operator carried on, so claiming it would resume work already done.\n353:  */\n354: function staleNoteText({ notePath } = {}) {\n355:   const pathValue = String(notePath ?? '<handoff-path>');\n356:   return [\n357:     '[session-handover] This session was compacted after its hand-over was withdrawn.',\n358:     `The handoff note at ${shellQuote(pathValue)} predates the work done since then.`,\n359:     'Read it for background only and do not claim it.',\n360:     'Update it at the next context nudge, which is when to hand over again.',\n361:   ].join(' ');\n362: }\n363: \n364: /** Check whether text starts with the relaunch seed marker. */\n365: function isSeedPrompt(text) {\n366:   return typeof text === 'string' && text.startsWith(SEED_PREFIX);\n367: }\n368: \n369: // The wrapper reads the same seed with the core parser, so both sides go through it and a\n370: // note path that holds the marker text cannot split one way here and another way there.\n371: /** Read the carried spec folder from a claim seed, or '' when it carries no usable answer. */\n372: function specFolderFromSeed(prompt) {\n373:   const parsed = core.parseClaimSeed(prompt);\n374:   return parsed ? parsed.specFolder : '';\n375: }\n376: \n377: // The runtime receives the seed path raw: its shell already consumed any\n378: // quoting, so an unescape or trim here would corrupt a path that holds a\n379: // real backslash or edge whitespace.\n380: /** Extract the raw handoff note path from a claim seed, or null when malformed. */\n381: function notePathFromSeed(prompt) {\n382:   const parsed = core.parseClaimSeed(prompt);\n383:   return parsed ? parsed.notePath : null;\n384: }\n385: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 386]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 200, \"offset\": 186, \"path\": \".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794808110912,"end":1794808111199}}}}
