{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794808239344,"sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2e828d0001WMxcGgRPARfbY2","sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","messageID":"msg_1e2e8118e0010HL4EK9wX2Mo5n","type":"tool","id":"call_00_s9716cnpfvvj7bz5dahpo76g","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"runId\":\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"The prepare text each runtime gives the sender and the claim text the receiver reads\",\"findingsCount\":8,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"All 8 findings are new to this packet: the shared prepare text was never read against the live Pi note, and the receiver's rendered claim output was read from its own session log.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"What does each runtime's prepare text tell the sender about keeping details out of the note, and does it over-promise what a fresh session can recover through the History Lookup?\",\"What claim text and History Lookup offer does the receiver read on OpenCode versus Pi, and what makes a receiver leave a claim unverified instead of running the lookup?\",\"How do the OpenCode and Pi session readers feed the History Lookup, including their tool-call argument shapes and secret redaction, and what does each fail to recover?\",\"Does model and effort carry on relaunch for each runtime, and where can it silently degrade or be dropped?\",\"Which known limits (OpenCode store without a directory column, AI_SESSION_CHILD leaking into test sandboxes, the 160-character preview cut, a double nudge from two hooks) cause a hop to fail, and what concrete fix addresses each?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"What does each runtime's prepare text tell the sender about keeping details out of the note, and does it over-promise what a fresh session can recover through the History Lookup?\",\"What claim text and History Lookup offer does the receiver read on OpenCode versus Pi, and what makes a receiver leave a claim unverified instead of running the lookup?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Pi did not mint or print the lookup section\",\"The Pi session reader could not find the sender session at claim time\",\"The shared prepare text differs between OpenCode and Pi\"],\"focusTrack\":\"handover-protocol-text\",\"edgeCase\":\"none\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:193\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:296\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:340\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/relaunch-core.cjs:1072\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts:82\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/README.md:198\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/note-20261116T053237Z-01a1e2d7-6b7b-75de-a705-ee16233b97a3.md:28\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/pane.txt:273\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/pane.txt:330\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-opencode/note-20261116T052759Z-ses_e1d2c7c81ffeJTAeWEY1UQO3wn.md:22\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-opencode/pane.txt:22\",\"~/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-422-opencode-pi-handover-parity--/2026-11-16T05-32-58-558Z_01a1e2d8-253d-75b7-978c-e205cabefd81.jsonl\"],\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q-prepare-text\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"Does the prepare text tell the sender what a fresh session can recover?\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q-claim-offer\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"What claim text and lookup offer does the receiver read?\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-prepare-no-lookup\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Shared prepare text never names the History Lookup\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-seed-no-step\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Claim seed has no lookup verification step\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-note-false-claim\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Pi note instructs the receiver to declare the detail unrecoverable\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-offer-printed\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"The claim printed a complete runnable lookup offer to the Pi receiver\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter001-1\",\"source\":\"f-prepare-no-lookup\",\"target\":\"q-prepare-text\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter001-2\",\"source\":\"f-seed-no-step\",\"target\":\"q-claim-offer\",\"relation\":\"SUPPORTS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter001-3\",\"source\":\"f-note-false-claim\",\"target\":\"q-claim-offer\",\"relation\":\"SUPPORTS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter001-4\",\"source\":\"f-offer-printed\",\"target\":\"f-note-false-claim\",\"relation\":\"CONTRADICTS\"}]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-001\",\"label\":\"Every runtime's prepare text is the same shared string, and it never mentions the History Lookup: handoffText lists the note shape, continuity save, fan-out/lock release and prepare, so a sender cannot learn that an omitted detail is recoverable.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:193\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-002\",\"label\":\"The claim-seed text, the receiver's first instruction set, has no lookup step: claim, read, resume, goal, active command, continue, complete, so a literal receiver can finish without opening the lookup.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:296\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:340\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-003\",\"label\":\"The Pi 4/5 note carries the sender's explicit false instruction to say plainly that a fresh session cannot recover the side word, which is the sentence the receiver obeyed.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/note-20261116T053237Z-01a1e2d7-6b7b-75de-a705-ee16233b97a3.md:28\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-004\",\"label\":\"The sender's recorded reasoning shows the false claim came from missing knowledge: it concluded the claim seed carries only the note path and spec folder and that recovery was literally impossible, having read only the README's first 175 lines and never its History Lookup section at line 198.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/pane.txt:273\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/README.md:198\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-005\",\"label\":\"The History Lookup offer was printed to the Pi receiver with a runnable browse command and the before-you-guess sentence; the receiver's own session log holds the rendered section, so this was not a minting, store or transaction failure.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/relaunch-core.cjs:1072\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts:82\",\"~/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-422-opencode-pi-handover-parity--/2026-11-16T05-32-58-558Z_01a1e2d8-253d-75b7-978c-e205cabefd81.jsonl\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-006\",\"label\":\"The Pi receiver asserted the opposite of the lookup's capability, saying there was no path through history lookup since the value was never written, when the side word sat in the sender's first user turn that the offered browse reads; a generic offer arriving after a note that says cannot-recover loses to the note.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/pane.txt:330\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-007\",\"label\":\"The parity difference is sender knowledge, not runtime prose: the OpenCode note pointed the receiver at the claim's History Lookup section and its receiver recovered the side word from the sender's first user turn, while both senders received the same shared prepare text.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-opencode/note-20261116T052759Z-ses_e1d2c7c81ffeJTAeWEY1UQO3wn.md:22\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-opencode/pane.txt:22\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:193\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter001-008\",\"label\":\"Nothing in the protocol gates completion on having checked the note's claims, so a false note claim survives to complete; on Pi the note stayed claimed only because the operator was asked.\",\"iteration\":1,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:340\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Pi did not mint or print the lookup section\",\"reason\":\"The receiver's session log contains the rendered section and an hl1_ handle.\",\"iteration\":1}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"The shared prepare text differs between OpenCode and Pi\",\"reason\":\"Both adapters call the same nudge.handoffText.\",\"iteration\":1}\n","path":"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deltas/iter-001.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deltas/iter-001.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deltas/iter-001.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":1,\\\"runId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\\\",\\\"lineageId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"target_agent\\\":\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"agent_definition_loaded\\\":true,\\\"resolved_route\\\":\\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\\"run\\\":1,\\\"status\\\":\\\"complete\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"The prepare text each runtime gives the sender and the claim text the receiver reads\\\",\\\"findingsCount\\\":8,\\\"newInfoRatio\\\":1.0,\\\"noveltyJustification\\\":\\\"All 8 findings are new to this packet: the shared prepare text was never read against the live Pi note, and the receiver's rendered claim output was read from its own session log.\\\",\\\"keyQuestions\\\":[\\\"What does each runtime's prepare text tell the sender about keeping details out of the note, and does it over-promise what a fresh session can recover through the History Lookup?\\\",\\\"What claim text and History Lookup offer does the receiver read on OpenCode versus Pi, and what makes a receiver leave a claim unverified instead of running the lookup?\\\",\\\"How do the OpenCode and Pi session readers feed the History Lookup, including their tool-call argument shapes and secret redaction, and what does each fail to recover?\\\",\\\"Does model and effort carry on relaunch for each runtime, and where can it silently degrade or be dropped?\\\",\\\"Which known limits (OpenCode store without a directory column, AI_SESSION_CHILD leaking into test sandboxes, the 160-character preview cut, a double nudge from two hooks) cause a hop to fail, and what concrete fix addresses each?\\\"],\\\"answeredQuestions\\\":[\\\"What does each runtime's prepare text tell the sender about keeping details out of the note, and does it over-promise what a fresh session can recover through the History Lookup?\\\",\\\"What claim text and History Lookup offer does the receiver read on OpenCode versus Pi, and what makes a receiver leave a claim unverified instead of running the lookup?\\\"],\\\"ruledOut\\\":[\\\"Pi did not mint or print the lookup section\\\",\\\"The Pi session reader could not find the sender session at claim time\\\",\\\"The shared prepare text differs between OpenCode and Pi\\\"],\\\"focusTrack\\\":\\\"handover-protocol-text\\\",\\\"edgeCase\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"toolsUsed\\\":[\\\"Read\\\",\\\"Grep\\\",\\\"Bash\\\"],\\\"sourcesQueried\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:193\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:296\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:340\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/relaunch-core.cjs:1072\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts:82\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/README.md:198\\\",\\\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-han