{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794808486597,"sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2ebf7b0002eUrdZJr4YLKXrf","sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","messageID":"msg_1e2ebed870015QOmjET0tCO14m","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ephkjbiz56l0hy97zh7ys3cr","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":3,\"runId\":\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":3,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Model and effort carry on relaunch, and the two-hook nudge\",\"findingsCount\":7,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"All 7 findings are new: carry is proven from the receiver's own session header, the scorecard's measurement gap is located, and the OpenCode 2 no-carry gate is pinned to a line.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"What does each runtime's prepare text tell the sender about keeping details out of the note, and does it over-promise what a fresh session can recover through the History Lookup?\",\"What claim text and History Lookup offer does the receiver read on OpenCode versus Pi, and what makes a receiver leave a claim unverified instead of running the lookup?\",\"How do the OpenCode and Pi session readers feed the History Lookup, including their tool-call argument shapes and secret redaction, and what does each fail to recover?\",\"Does model and effort carry on relaunch for each runtime, and where can it silently degrade or be dropped?\",\"Which known limits (OpenCode store without a directory column, AI_SESSION_CHILD leaking into test sandboxes, the 160-character preview cut, a double nudge from two hooks) cause a hop to fail, and what concrete fix addresses each?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"Does model and effort carry on relaunch for each runtime, and where can it silently degrade or be dropped?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Pi dropped the model or effort on relaunch\",\"The two Pi nudge hooks can both deliver the same text\",\"OpenCode 2's missing model flag is a replay-builder bug\"],\"focusTrack\":\"relaunch-carry\",\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\",\"Bash\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:459\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:594\",\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:620\",\".skilled/bin/skilled-loop:778\",\".opencode/plugins/session-handover.js:590\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/harness/score.cjs:60\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/relaunch.log:3\",\"~/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-422-opencode-pi-handover-parity--/2026-11-16T05-32-58-558Z_01a1e2d8-253d-75b7-978c-e205cabefd81.jsonl\"],\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"q-carry\",\"kind\":\"QUESTION\",\"label\":\"Does model and effort carry on relaunch?\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-carry-worked-pi\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Pi carried model and max thinking into the receiver\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-carry-unmeasured\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"The scorecard reads argv and cannot see Pi's carry\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-opencode2-no-carry\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"OpenCode 2 replays neither model nor effort\"},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"f-nudge-level-spent-early\",\"kind\":\"FINDING\",\"label\":\"Pi spends the nudge level before delivery\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter003-1\",\"source\":\"f-carry-worked-pi\",\"target\":\"q-carry\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter003-2\",\"source\":\"f-opencode2-no-carry\",\"target\":\"q-carry\",\"relation\":\"ANSWERS\"},{\"type\":\"edge\",\"id\":\"e-iter003-3\",\"source\":\"f-carry-unmeasured\",\"target\":\"f-carry-worked-pi\",\"relation\":\"CONTRADICTS\"}]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-001\",\"label\":\"Model and effort did carry on the live Pi hop: the receiver session header records model_change to llmgateway deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 and thinking_level_change to max, matching the sender, so the Pi 4/5 is not a carry failure.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:459\",\"~/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-422-opencode-pi-handover-parity--/2026-11-16T05-32-58-558Z_01a1e2d8-253d-75b7-978c-e205cabefd81.jsonl\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-002\",\"label\":\"The scorecard's unobservable carry is a measurement gap: it reads model, effort, name and provider from the receiver argv and marks everything unobservable when the first launch argv is a bare runtime name, which Pi always is, and it never reads the receiver session header.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/harness/score.cjs:60\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/argv.log:2\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-003\",\"label\":\"After a hop nothing durable records the relaunch values: relaunch.log carries only loop id and reason, and the relaunch record is consumed and removed, so a silent drop and a carried value look identical in the artifacts a hop leaves behind.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/relaunch.log:3\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-004\",\"label\":\"OpenCode 2 carries neither model nor effort by design: the wrapper appends -m only when the runtime is not OpenCode 2 and the effort appender has branches for Claude, Codex and Pi only, so a receiver starts on the configured default and the 5/5 run matched only because the default was the same model.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/bin/skilled-loop:778\",\".skilled/bin/skilled-loop:399\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-005\",\"label\":\"Pi spends the nudge level before the nudge is delivered: message_end stores the text in an in-memory map and writes the level, delivery happens later on turn_end or agent_end, so a host reload or a run ending in between loses the text with the level already spent and the session is never nudged at that level again.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:594\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-006\",\"label\":\"The two Pi nudge hooks cannot double-deliver because the held text is deleted from the map before sendMessage, so turn_end and agent_end race but only one delivers; the uncovered Pi risk is loss, not repetition.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:620\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter003-007\",\"label\":\"OpenCode computes the nudge in its event hook and delivers it in experimental.chat.system.transform, guarded by pendingNudge and handoffPending; a session that claimed a note keeps claimedReminder every request and can simultaneously receive a fresh hand-over nudge once its own fill crosses the threshold, so one system prompt carries two instructions.\",\"iteration\":3,\"sources\":[\".opencode/plugins/session-handover.js:590\",\".opencode/plugins/session-handover.js:180\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Pi dropped the model or effort on relaunch\",\"reason\":\"The receiver session header shows model_change and thinking_level_change to the sender values.\",\"iteration\":3}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"The two Pi nudge hooks can both deliver the same text\",\"reason\":\"deliverHeldNudge deletes the map entry before sendMessage.\",\"iteration\":3}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"OpenCode 2's missing model flag is a replay-builder bug\",\"reason\":\"The version gate is deliberate: a replayed -m would end the OpenCode 2 launch with a usage error.\",\"iteration\":3}\n","path":"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deltas/iter-003.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deltas/iter-003.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deltas/iter-003.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"runId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\\\",\\\"lineageId\\\":\\\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"target_agent\\\":\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"agent_definition_loaded\\\":true,\\\"resolved_route\\\":\\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\\"run\\\":3,\\\"status\\\":\\\"complete\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"Model and effort carry on relaunch, and the two-hook nudge\\\",\\\"findingsCount\\\":7,\\\"newInfoRatio\\\":1.0,\\\"noveltyJustification\\\":\\\"All 7 findings are new: carry is proven from the receiver's own session header, the scorecard's measurement gap is located, and the OpenCode 2 no-carry gate is pinned to a line.\\\",\\\"keyQuestions\\\":[\\\"What does each runtime's prepare text tell the sender about keeping details out of the note, and does it over-promise what a fresh session can recover through the History Lookup?\\\",\\\"What claim text and History Lookup offer does the receiver read on OpenCode versus Pi, and what makes a receiver leave a claim unverified instead of running the lookup?\\\",\\\"How do the OpenCode and Pi session readers feed the History Lookup, including their tool-call argument shapes and secret redaction, and what does each fail to recover?\\\",\\\"Does model and effort carry on relaunch for each runtime, and where can it silently degrade or be dropped?\\\",\\\"Which known limits (OpenCode store without a directory column, AI_SESSION_CHILD leaking into test sandboxes, the 160-character preview cut, a double nudge from two hooks) cause a hop to fail, and what concrete fix addresses each?\\\"],\\\"answeredQuestions\\\":[\\\"Does model and effort carry on relaunch for each runtime, and where can it silently degrade or be dropped?\\\"],\\\"ruledOut\\\":[\\\"Pi dropped the model or effort on relaunch\\\",\\\"The two Pi nudge hooks can both deliver the same text\\\",\\\"OpenCode 2's missing model flag is a replay-builder bug\\\"],\\\"focusTrack\\\":\\\"relaunch-carry\\\",\\\"edgeCase\\\":\\\"contradictory-evidence\\\",\\\"toolsUsed\\\":[\\\"Read\\\",\\\"Grep\\\",\\\"Bash\\\"],\\\"sourcesQueried\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:459\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:594\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:620\\\",\\\".skilled/bin/skilled-loop:778\\\",\\\".opencode/plugins/session-handover.js:590\\\",\\\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/harness/score.cjs:60\\\",\\\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/relaunch.log:3\\\",\\\"~/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-422-opencode-pi-handover-parity--/2026-11-16T05-32-58-558Z_01a1e2d8-253d-75b7-978c-e205cabefd81.jsonl\\\"],\\\"graphEvents\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"q-carry\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"QUESTION\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Does model and effort carry on relaunch?\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-carry-worked-pi\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Pi carried model and max thinking into the receiver\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-carry-unmeasured\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The scorecard reads argv and cannot see Pi's carry\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-opencode2-no-carry\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"OpenCode 2 replays neither model nor effort\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"node\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-nudge-level-spent-early\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"FINDING\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Pi spends the nudge level before delivery\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-iter003-1\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-carry-worked-pi\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q-carry\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-iter003-2\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-opencode2-no-carry\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"q-carry\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"ANSWERS\\\"},{\\\"type\\\":\\\"edge\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"e-iter003-3\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"f-carry-unmeasured\\\",\\\"target\\\":\\\"f-carry-worked-pi\\\",\\\"relation\\\":\\\"CONTRADICTS\\\"}]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-001\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Model and effort did carry on the live Pi hop: the receiver session header records model_change to llmgateway deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 and thinking_level_change to max, matching the sender, so the Pi 4/5 is not a carry failure.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:459\\\",\\\"~/.pi/agent/sessions/--Users-michelkerkmeester-worktrees-public-422-opencode-pi-handover-parity--/2026-11-16T05-32-58-558Z_01a1e2d8-253d-75b7-978c-e205cabefd81.jsonl\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-002\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The scorecard's unobservable carry is a measurement gap: it reads model, effort, name and provider from the receiver argv and marks everything unobservable when the first launch argv is a bare runtime name, which Pi always is, and it never reads the receiver session header.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/harness/score.cjs:60\\\",\\\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/argv.log:2\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-003\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"After a hop nothing durable records the relaunch values: relaunch.log carries only loop id and reason, and the relaunch record is consumed and removed, so a silent drop and a carried value look identical in the artifacts a hop leaves behind.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/relaunch.log:3\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-004\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"OpenCode 2 carries neither model nor effort by design: the wrapper appends -m only when the runtime is not OpenCode 2 and the effort appender has branches for Claude, Codex and Pi only, so a receiver starts on the configured default and the 5/5 run matched only because the default was the same model.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/bin/skilled-loop:778\\\",\\\".skilled/bin/skilled-loop:399\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-005\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Pi spends the nudge level before the nudge is delivered: message_end stores the text in an in-memory map and writes the level, delivery happens later on turn_end or agent_end, so a host reload or a run ending in between loses the text with the level already spent and the session is never nudged at that level again.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:594\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-006\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The two Pi nudge hooks cannot double-deliver because the held text is deleted from the map before sendMessage, so turn_end and agent_end race but only one delivers; the uncovered Pi risk is loss, not repetition.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:620\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter003-007\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"OpenCode computes the nudge in its event hook and delivers it in experimental.chat.system.transform, guarded by pendingNudge and handoffPending; a session that claimed a note keeps claimedReminder every request and can simultaneously receive a fresh hand-over nudge once its own fill crosses the threshold, so one system prompt carries two instructions.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".opencode/plugins/session-handover.js:590\\\",\\\".opencode/plugins/session-handover.js:180\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"Pi dropped the model or effort on relaunch\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The receiver session header shows model_change and thinking_level_change to the sender values.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"The two Pi nudge hooks can both deliver the same text\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"deliverHeldNudge deletes the map entry before sendMessage.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"OpenCode 2's missing model flag is a replay-builder bug\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The version gate is deliberate: a replayed -m would end the OpenCode 2 launch with a usage error.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":3}\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deltas/iter-003.jsonl\"}"},"time":{"start":1794808477616,"end":1794808486597}}}}
