T and SKILLED_LOOP_CLAIM_SEED only, so a receiver inherits the flag from whatever launched the wrapper.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/bin/skilled-loop:911\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter004-003\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The live-hop harness unsets SKILLED_LOOP_HOPS, SKILLED_LOOP_ID, CLAUDECODE and CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID but not AI_SESSION_CHILD, so a harness run started from a dispatched worker produces a sender that is never nudged.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/harness/live-hop.sh:63\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter004-004\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The base1 runs prove the leak was absent there rather than impossible: both senders were nudged and prepared, which cannot happen with the flag set, so a rerun from inside a dispatched worker or fan-out child would measure a session that never hands over.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/relaunch.log:1\\\",\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:704\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter004-005\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The damage is asymmetric: the sender loses the nudge, but seedInstructions builds the claim text with no child check, so a receiver that inherits the flag still receives and can still claim, which means the leak breaks the start of a hop and not the claim of one already started.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:389\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"The child flag suppresses only the claim\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"The nudge is the suppressed path and the claim path has no check at all.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"The harness's unset list is a general environment sanitizer\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"It names four specific variables plus a Vibe key, so every other inherited flag passes through.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":4}\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deltas/iter-004.jsonl\"}"},"time":{"start":1794808554128,"end":1794808560773}}}}
