urceMapSkipped\": null,\n  \"resourceMapSkipReason\": null,\n  \"deltaSourceCount\": null\n}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"ok\":true,\"receipt\":{\"ledger_id\":\"deep-research-ledger\",\"sequence\":5,\"event_id\":\"event-14db1bb7-52c5-4821-b6ee-ff917d58a029\",\"event_type\":\"deep-research.ledger.iteration-completed\",\"event_version\":1,\"stream_id\":\"deep-research-ledger\",\"stream_sequence\":5,\"committed_at\":\"2026-11-16T05:56:06.938Z\",\"canonicalEventHash\":\"97b3319ed15ddb7ceb6484f2f710e60f664f5a6e242fa4d8b14139d891d42a13\",\"recordHash\":\"59b573a009d3816d1a2d8013eb31f8a1a56d49817e9196ff5d3f0fcbc260d722\",\"authorizationRef\":{\"audit_ledger_id\":\"deep-research-audit-ledger\",\"audit_sequence\":6,\"audit_record_hash\":\"519568761c899055b0a688ab23287bd861686a0e8dbb8ae79a880e42bb7f3fb1\",\"decision_id\":\"decision-77656d36-6419-4013-a26e-e0c682998c44\",\"decision_digest\":\"877112fa43ba270e8c43f45d7450d2c3f2e21c6fdda465f4a2e3c2fced7a18e2\",\"request_digest\":\"1d532c56fb07f004950b3633cf38ecd85471ac7a3c56de1fbf80d1eceed9d39f\",\"policy_digest\":\"a4b1c20c36f40aa5f6c82a50e7fb20354deda901fb7b2be8f51dc112f221c7dd\",\"authority_epoch\":1,\"fence_token\":5},\"ledgerId\":\"deep-research-ledger\",\"eventId\":\"event-14db1bb7-52c5-4821-b6ee-ff917d58a029\",\"eventType\":\"deep-research.ledger.iteration-completed\",\"eventVersion\":1,\"streamId\":\"deep-research-ledger\",\"streamSequence\":5,\"committedAt\":\"2026-11-16T05:56:06.938Z\"},\"projectionRefreshed\":true,\"projectionError\":null,\"warnings\":[\"Trusted evidence yield was absent and remains explicitly zero.\"]}\nGATEWAY_EXIT=0\n  \"registryPath\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity/specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/findings-registry.json\",\n  \"dashboardPath\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity/specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deep-research-dashboard.md\",\n  \"strategyPath\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity/specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\",\n  \"iterationsCompleted\": 4,\n  \"corruptionCount\": 0,\n  \"resourceMapPath\": null,\n  \"resourceMapSkipped\": null,\n  \"resourceMapSkipReason\": null,\n  \"deltaSourceCount\": null\n}\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity && LINEAGE_ABS=\\\"$PWD/specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek\\\" && EVENT_FILE=\\\"$(mktemp \\\"${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/deep-research-iteration-004.XXXXXX\\\")\\\" && node -e '\\nconst fs=require(\\\"fs\\\");\\nconst delta=fs.readFileSync(process.argv[1],\\\"utf8\\\").split(\\\"\\\\n\\\").filter(Boolean);\\nfs.writeFileSync(process.argv[2], delta[0], \\\"utf8\\\");\\n' \\\"$LINEAGE_ABS/deltas/iter-004.jsonl\\\" \\\"$EVENT_FILE\\\" && node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode research --run-directory \\\"$LINEAGE_ABS\\\" --event-json \\\"$EVENT_FILE\\\"; STATUS=$?; rm -f \\\"$EVENT_FILE\\\"; echo \\\"GATEWAY_EXIT=$STATUS\\\" && node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity --artifact-dir specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek 2>&1 | tail -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794808565017,"end":1794808567306}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794808568642,"sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","part":{"id":"prt_1e2ed5b42001jCgnzPdCLD6Dr6","sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","messageID":"msg_1e2ed4308001Hci0tppKumV3zF","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"c00c5d2c049bc45ebf03d96ab365809d62778736","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":1851,"output":392,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":225536,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794808571565,"sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","part":{"id":"prt_1e2ed66ad001uZI1lZ7xciCwnU","sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","messageID":"msg_1e2ed5b48001sS3K3trFh6h5Hz","type":"step-start","snapshot":"c00c5d2c049bc45ebf03d96ab365809d62778736"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794808593679,"sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2ed859b001vloSmxb9Bzc2Ah","sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","messageID":"msg_1e2ed5b48001sS3K3trFh6h5Hz","type":"tool","id":"call_00_czmeh3d7lxrlgiabyu01dw09","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: The Fix Set (One Concrete Change Per Failure Mode)\n\n## Focus\n\nTurn the failure modes recorded in iterations 1 to 4 into one concrete change each, naming the file and function and the observable that would prove the fix. This is the analytical pass the fifth key question asks for; no new external source was needed beyond the lines already cited, each re-read at its named location.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n- Re-read each cited location against the fix it implies.\n- Ordered the fixes by whether they change what the sender knows, what the receiver is told, what the reader can return, or what the run can prove.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Sender over-promise.** Change `handoffText` in `.skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs` to state that a detail kept out of the note is still recoverable by the receiver through the claim's History Lookup, and to forbid the sender from writing that a fresh session cannot recover it. Observable: a hop whose note deliberately omits a value no longer contains an \"unrecoverable\" instruction, and the receiver recovers the value. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:193]\n\n2. **No verification step in the seed.** Add one step to `seedText` before \"Continue the work\": when Remaining work names a detail the note does not carry, run the printed History Lookup before asking the operator or closing the note. Observable: the receiver's transcript shows a `history-lookup.mjs` call before any operator question. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:296]\n\n3. **The offer loses to the note.** Add one sentence to `buildHistoryLookupBody` in `.skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts`: the note is not authoritative about what the sender's history holds, so try the lookup before concluding a detail is unrecoverable. Observable: a receiver facing a note that says \"cannot recover\" runs the lookup instead of repeating the note's claim. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts:82]\n\n4. **Preview cut.** Make `browse` previews carry the whole first part up to the reply budget, or attach an explicit `load` pointer to every reference in the browse reply. Observable: the live prompt's side word at character 295 appears in a browse reply without a second call. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/navigator.ts:265]\n\n5. **Arguments dropped by shape.** Change `toolCallBlock` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/project.mjs` to preserve a string argument, for example by parsing JSON or keeping it under a value key, instead of replacing it with `{}`. Observable: a session whose tool input is a JSON string returns the input in a loaded turn. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/project.mjs:40]\n\n6. **One bad pair costs the session.** Give projection defects their own refusal code and skip the offending pair instead of failing the read, in `projectEntries` and the dispatcher's `readSession` mapping. Observable: a session with one orphaned tool result still returns every other turn, and the refusal code names the pairing rather than the store. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:127]\n\n7. **Folder proof on OpenCode.** When the session table has no `directory` column, fail closed at mint (`readerFindsSession`) or record the folder on the locator at arm time and verify it against store metadata, in `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/opencode.mjs`. Observable: a note from another folder gets no lookup offer rather than another project's turns. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/opencode.mjs:256]\n\n8. **Pi cwd keying.** Record the Pi store key on the locator at mint and fall back to an exact-id scan of project directories when the note's `cwd` misses, in `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs`. Observable: a session started in a subdirectory is still found when the note records a later cwd. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:222]\n\n9. **Carry cannot be audited.** Append one `relaunch-args` line to `relaunch.log` from `skilled-loop` with model, provider, effort and name, and have `score.cjs` read a Pi receiver's session header for the same fields. Observable: `carry` reads `kept` or `dropped`, never `unobservable`. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:744]\n\n10. **OpenCode 2 starts on the default.** There is no model flag to replay, so emit one warning line when the receiver's effective model differs from the sender's, and state the limitation in the runtime matrix. Observable: an OpenCode 2 hop that changed model prints the warning instead of passing silently. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:778]\n\n11. **Pi loses a held nudge.** Persist the held text, or defer the `writeState` level bump until delivery, in `.skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts`, and deliver any held text on the next `agent_settled`. Observable: a host reload between hold and delivery still produces the nudge. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:594]\n\n12. **The child flag leaks.** Unset `AI_SESSION_CHILD` in `skilled-loop` before launching a runtime and in the live-hop harness's `tmux` line, so the flag describes the worker that owns it and never the session it launches. Observable: a hop started from a dispatched worker still nudges, prepares and claims. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:911]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- \"Fix the model by making the receiver read the note harder\": ruled out by iteration 1. The receiver read the note exactly; the note was wrong, and the offer arrived without authority over it.\n- \"Fix the preview by raising it without limit\": ruled out as a design choice; the reply budget is what keeps the lookup inside a model-visible payload. The bounded fix is a load pointer or whole-part preview inside the same budget.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Any fix that only changes documentation: the README already documents the lookup correctly and the sender never reads it at the hand-over moment.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"concrete fix\" could mean a patch or a direction. Chose one function per fix plus an observable, without editing the researched code.\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: fixing 1 to 3 changes the text path; 4 to 8 change the reader path; 9 to 12 change evidence and environment. A partial application still yields a measurable improvement, but only 1 to 3 address the recorded 4/5 case directly.\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- Which known limits (OpenCode store without a directory column, AI_SESSION_CHILD leaking into test sandboxes, the 160-character preview cut, a double nudge from two hooks) cause a hop to fail, and what concrete fix addresses each?\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\nNone. All five key questions now have cited answers.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:193\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:296\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts:82\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/navigator.ts:265\n- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/project.mjs:40\n- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:127\n- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/opencode.mjs:256\n- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:222\n- .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:744\n- .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:778\n- .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:911\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:594\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:620\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.6\n- Questions addressed: the known-limits fix set\n- Questions answered: known limits and their fixes\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: ordering the fixes by the layer they change (sender text, receiver text, reader, evidence) kept each one attributable to a single recorded failure instead of producing a wish list.\n- What did not work and why: an early attempt to write one combined \"protocol hardening\" fix collapsed four distinct causes into one unverifiable change; split per failure mode is what makes each observable.\n- What I would do differently: state the observable before the change. Two candidate fixes (raise the preview, add a lookup step) only became precise once the observable was named.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nSynthesis. All five questions are answered; the remaining work is to consolidate the findings into one report, keep the fix set attached to its evidence, and record the convergence outcome.\n","path":"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 5: The Fix Set (One Concrete Change Per Failure Mode)\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nTurn the failure modes recorded in iterations 1 to 4 into one concrete change each, naming the file and function and the observable that would prove the fix. This is the analytical pass the fifth key question asks for; no new external source was needed beyond the lines already cited, each re-read at its named location.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n- Re-read each cited location against the fix it implies.\\n- Ordered the fixes by whether they change what the sender knows, what the receiver is told, what the reader can return, or what the run can prove.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **Sender over-promise.** Change `handoffText` in `.skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs` to state that a detail kept out of the note is still recoverable by the receiver through the claim's History Lookup, and to forbid the sender from writing that a fresh session cannot recover it. Observable: a hop whose note deliberately omits a value no longer contains an \\\"unrecoverable\\\" instruction, and the receiver recovers the value. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:193]\\n\\n2. **No verification step in the seed.** Add one step to `seedText` before \\\"Continue the work\\\": when Remaining work names a detail the note does not carry, run the printed History Lookup before asking the operator or closing the note. Observable: the receiver's transcript shows a `history-lookup.mjs` call before any operator question. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:296]\\n\\n3. **The offer loses to the note.** Add one sentence to `buildHistoryLookupBody` in `.skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts`: the note is not authoritative about what the sender's history holds, so try the lookup before concluding a detail is unrecoverable. Observable: a receiver facing a note that says \\\"cannot recover\\\" runs the lookup instead of repeating the note's claim. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts:82]\\n\\n4. **Preview cut.** Make `browse` previews carry the whole first part up to the reply budget, or attach an explicit `load` pointer to every reference in the browse reply. Observable: the live prompt's side word at character 295 appears in a browse reply without a second call. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/navigator.ts:265]\\n\\n5. **Arguments dropped by shape.** Change `toolCallBlock` in `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/project.mjs` to preserve a string argument, for example by parsing JSON or keeping it under a value key, instead of replacing it with `{}`. Observable: a session whose tool input is a JSON string returns the input in a loaded turn. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/project.mjs:40]\\n\\n6. **One bad pair costs the session.** Give projection defects their own refusal code and skip the offending pair instead of failing the read, in `projectEntries` and the dispatcher's `readSession` mapping. Observable: a session with one orphaned tool result still returns every other turn, and the refusal code names the pairing rather than the store. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:127]\\n\\n7. **Folder proof on OpenCode.** When the session table has no `directory` column, fail closed at mint (`readerFindsSession`) or record the folder on the locator at arm time and verify it against store metadata, in `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/opencode.mjs`. Observable: a note from another folder gets no lookup offer rather than another project's turns. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/opencode.mjs:256]\\n\\n8. **Pi cwd keying.** Record the Pi store key on the locator at mint and fall back to an exact-id scan of project directories when the note's `cwd` misses, in `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs`. Observable: a session started in a subdirectory is still found when the note records a later cwd. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:222]\\n\\n9. **Carry cannot be audited.** Append one `relaunch-args` line to `relaunch.log` from `skilled-loop` with model, provider, effort and name, and have `score.cjs` read a Pi receiver's session header for the same fields. Observable: `carry` reads `kept` or `dropped`, never `unobservable`. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:744]\\n\\n10. **OpenCode 2 starts on the default.** There is no model flag to replay, so emit one warning line when the receiver's effective model differs from the sender's, and state the limitation in the runtime matrix. Observable: an OpenCode 2 hop that changed model prints the warning instead of passing silently. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:778]\\n\\n11. **Pi loses a held nudge.** Persist the held text, or defer the `writeState` level bump until delivery, in `.skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts`, and deliver any held text on the next `agent_settled`. Observable: a host reload between hold and delivery still produces the nudge. [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:594]\\n\\n12. **The child flag leaks.** Unset `AI_SESSION_CHILD` in `skilled-loop` before launching a runtime and in the live-hop harness's `tmux` line, so the flag describes the worker that owns it and never the session it launches. Observable: a hop started from a dispatched worker still nudges, prepares and claims. [SOURCE: .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:911]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- \\\"Fix the model by making the receiver read the note harder\\\": ruled out by iteration 1. The receiver read the note exactly; the note was wrong, and the offer arrived without authority over it.\\n- \\\"Fix the preview by raising it without limit\\\": ruled out as a design choice; the reply budget is what keeps the lookup inside a model-visible payload. The bounded fix is a load pointer or whole-part preview inside the same budget.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Any fix that only changes documentation: the README already documents the lookup correctly and the sender never reads it at the hand-over moment.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"concrete fix\\\" could mean a patch or a direction. Chose one function per fix plus an observable, without editing the researched code.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\\n- Missing dependencies: none.\\n- Partial success: fixing 1 to 3 changes the text path; 4 to 8 change the reader path; 9 to 12 change evidence and environment. A partial application still yields a measurable improvement, but only 1 to 3 address the recorded 4/5 case directly.\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- Which known limits (OpenCode store without a directory column, AI_SESSION_CHILD leaking into test sandboxes, the 160-character preview cut, a double nudge from two hooks) cause a hop to fail, and what concrete fix addresses each?\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\nNone. All five key questions now have cited answers.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:193\\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/lib/nudge.cjs:296\\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/lookup-offer.ts:82\\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/history/lib/navigator.ts:265\\n- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/project.mjs:40\\n- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:127\\n- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/opencode.mjs:256\\n- .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:222\\n- .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:744\\n- .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:778\\n- .skilled/bin/skilled-loop:911\\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:594\\n- .skilled/hooks/session-handover/pi/session-handover.ts:620\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.6\\n- Questions addressed: the known-limits fix set\\n- Questions answered: known limits and their fixes\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: ordering the fixes by the layer they change (sender text, receiver text, reader, evidence) kept each one attributable to a single recorded failure instead of producing a wish list.\\n- What did not work and why: an early attempt to write one combined \\\"protocol hardening\\\" fix collapsed four distinct causes into one unverifiable change; split per failure mode is what makes each observable.\\n- What I would do differently: state the observable before the change. Two candidate fixes (raise the preview, add a lookup step) only became precise once the observable was named.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nSynthesis. All five questions are answered; the remaining work is to consolidate the findings into one report, keep the fix set attached to its evidence, and record the convergence outcome.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794808579483,"end":1794808593679}}}}
