{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794808770615,"sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2f02e14002Z6I4r0OC10Mlg2","sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","messageID":"msg_1e2effc05001phqIzbBeijWegF","type":"tool","id":"call_00_5ad2kqlv1r93v6q1q1vou228","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":6,\"runId\":\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-opencode-go-deepseek-1794807924469-5jb1x3\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":6,\"status\":\"insight\",\"focus\":\"Evidence classes and the source ledger for all five answered questions\",\"findingsCount\":3,\"newInfoRatio\":0.75,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Two findings are fully new (the source-class guard and the three-artifact agreement) and one is partially new (the two remaining inferences, now labelled); the pass also records a cleaner model of the evidence base, earning the simplicity bonus.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"What does each runtime's prepare text tell the sender about keeping details out of the note, and does it over-promise what a fresh session can recover through the History Lookup?\",\"What claim text and History Lookup offer does the receiver read on OpenCode versus Pi, and what makes a receiver leave a claim unverified instead of running the lookup?\",\"How do the OpenCode and Pi session readers feed the History Lookup, including their tool-call argument shapes and secret redaction, and what does each fail to recover?\",\"Does model and effort carry on relaunch for each runtime, and where can it silently degrade or be dropped?\",\"Which known limits (OpenCode store without a directory column, AI_SESSION_CHILD leaking into test sandboxes, the 160-character preview cut, a double nudge from two hooks) cause a hop to fail, and what concrete fix addresses each?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"ruledOut\":[\"Source diversity means counting files\",\"The blocked stop was a false positive to be argued past\"],\"focusTrack\":\"evidence-coverage\",\"edgeCase\":\"none\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Grep\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts:653\",\".skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:222\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/pane.txt:330\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/note-20261116T053237Z-01a1e2d7-6b7b-75de-a705-ee16233b97a3.md:28\",\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/harness/live-hop.sh:63\"],\"graphEvents\":[{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"src-run-note-pi\",\"kind\":\"SOURCE\",\"label\":\"Pi sender handoff note\",\"path\":\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/note-20261116T053237Z-01a1e2d7-6b7b-75de-a705-ee16233b97a3.md\",\"metadata\":{\"quality_class\":\"primary\",\"kind\":\"run-artifact\"}},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"src-run-pane-pi\",\"kind\":\"SOURCE\",\"label\":\"Pi sender and receiver pane capture\",\"path\":\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-pi-handover-parity/scratch/runs/base1-pi/pane.txt\",\"metadata\":{\"quality_class\":\"primary\",\"kind\":\"run-artifact\"}},{\"type\":\"node\",\"id\":\"src-run-meta-pi\",\"kind\":\"SOURCE\",\"label\":\"Pi run metadata with launch prompt\",\"path\":\"specs/hooks-plugins-extensions/session-handover/001-history-lookup-handover-integration/011-opencode-p