{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794808865378,"sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","part":{"partID":"prt_1e2f1dfd20021bYvA0l55Of4rz","sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","messageID":"msg_1e2f1bb91001jDV1BfAHPmWmd2","type":"tool","id":"call_00_y3sienmh8xe6nggteqx98ysx","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity && grep -n \"function computeResearchQuestionCoverageFromData\" -A 30 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts; echo \"=== blockers ===\"; grep -rn \"uncovered_questions\\|source_diversity_guard\" --include=\"*.ts\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph | head"},"output":"570:export function computeResearchQuestionCoverageFromData(\n571-  nodes: ReadonlyArray<ResearchSignalNodeLike>,\n572-  edges: ReadonlyArray<ResearchSignalEdgeLike>,\n573-): number {\n574-  const questionIds = nodes\n575-    .filter(node => node.kind === 'QUESTION')\n576-    .map(node => node.id);\n577-\n578-  if (questionIds.length === 0) return 0;\n579-\n580-  const answeringFindings = buildAnsweringFindingsByQuestion(edges);\n581-  let coveredQuestions = 0;\n582-\n583-  for (const questionId of questionIds) {\n584-    if ((answeringFindings.get(questionId) ?? []).length >= 2) {\n585-      coveredQuestions++;\n586-    }\n587-  }\n588-\n589-  return coveredQuestions / questionIds.length;\n590-}\n591-\n592-/**\n593- * Canonical research claim verification rate: verified claims divided by all\n594- * claim nodes, where verified means verification_status exists and is not\n595- * \"unresolved\".\n596- *\n597- * Zero claim nodes is a vacuous pass (returns 1.0): there is nothing to verify,\n598- * so this signal must not block convergence. Returning 0 would mark the trace\n599- * entry failed and force a claimless-but-otherwise-converged graph to loop\n600- * forever, since no unverified-claims blocker is raised for the empty case.\n=== blockers ===\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"570:export function computeResearchQuestionCoverageFromData(\n571-  nodes: ReadonlyArray<ResearchSignalNodeLike>,\n572-  edges: ReadonlyArray<ResearchSignalEdgeLike>,\n573-): number {\n574-  const questionIds = nodes\n575-    .filter(node => node.kind === 'QUESTION')\n576-    .map(node => node.id);\n577-\n578-  if (questionIds.length === 0) return 0;\n579-\n580-  const answeringFindings = buildAnsweringFindingsByQuestion(edges);\n581-  let coveredQuestions = 0;\n582-\n583-  for (const questionId of questionIds) {\n584-    if ((answeringFindings.get(questionId) ?? []).length >= 2) {\n585-      coveredQuestions++;\n586-    }\n587-  }\n588-\n589-  return coveredQuestions / questionIds.length;\n590-}\n591-\n592-/**\n593- * Canonical research claim verification rate: verified claims divided by all\n594- * claim nodes, where verified means verification_status exists and is not\n595- * \"unresolved\".\n596- *\n597- * Zero claim nodes is a vacuous pass (returns 1.0): there is nothing to verify,\n598- * so this signal must not block convergence. Returning 0 would mark the trace\n599- * entry failed and force a claimless-but-otherwise-converged graph to loop\n600- * forever, since no unverified-claims blocker is raised for the empty case.\n=== blockers ===\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/422-opencode-pi-handover-parity && grep -n \\\"function computeResearchQuestionCoverageFromData\\\" -A 30 .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph/coverage-graph-signals.ts; echo \\\"=== blockers ===\\\"; grep -rn \\\"uncovered_questions\\\\|source_diversity_guard\\\" --include=\\\"*.ts\\\" .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/coverage-graph | head\"}"},"time":{"start":1794808864722,"end":1794808