{"type":"text","timestamp":1794809075678,"sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","part":{"id":"prt_1e2f50aa9002blBnRsPJjO81cJ","sessionID":"ses_e1d1c612bffenqRaMYnBfMfTGv","messageID":"msg_1e2f4fb4900166ghDbo12D8Gli","type":"text","text":"## Lineage `opencode-go-deepseek` — complete\n\n**Converged** after 8 iterations (`all_questions_answered`, graph `STOP_ALLOWED`; coverage 1.0, source diversity 2.0, evidence depth 2.0). 47 cited findings, 5/5 key questions resolved, 26 sources mapped.\n\n**Core result.** The Pi 4/5 was not a runtime or carry failure. The shared prepare text never names the History Lookup (`nudge.cjs:193`), so the sender wrote \"a fresh session cannot recover it\" into the note (`base1-pi` note:28). The claim *did* print a complete runnable offer — it is in the receiver's own session store — but the claim seed has no verification step and the offer carries no authority against the note, so the receiver declared history useless without running it (`pane.txt:330`). OpenCode's sender had read the README's lookup section and pointed its receiver at the lookup, which recovered the same side word.\n\n**Other defects found:** browse previews cut at 160 chars while the live side word sits at 295; one bad tool-result pair reports the whole session as `store_unreadable`; non-object tool arguments become `{}`; OpenCode without a `directory` column cannot prove the session folder; OpenCode 2 carries neither model nor effort while Pi's carry works but is invisible to the argv-based scorecard; Pi spends the nudge level before delivery; `AI_SESSION_CHILD` removes the nudge entirely and neither the wrapper nor the harness scrubs it.\n\n**Deliverables** (all under `research/lineages/opencode-go-deepseek/`): `research.md` (with fix table, eliminated alternatives, divergence map, containment note), `resource-map.md`, 8 iterations, 8 deltas, strategy/dashboard/registry, and 10 gateway receipts in the ledger.\n\n**Containment:** checksum diff against the lineage baseline reports no packet file changed. The resource-map command ignored `--artifact-dir` and wrote into the parent packet; that stray file was removed to restore the baseline, and the map was regenerated inside the lineage. Continuity save was skipped because it writes outside the lineage; no git writes were run.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:opencode-go-deepseek","time":{"start":1794809072297,"end":1794809075678}}}
